; Interprets: RFC 4005
;; What RFC 4005's clauses state in prose about an AVP's value or presence,
;; read by hand and pinned to the sentences read (docs/constraints.md), in
;; clause order. RFC 7155 obsoletes the document, and its own file reads
;; RFC 7155's text. A block with no scope, or within a grouped AVP, holds
;; wherever a document reading RFC 4005's AVP reads it; a block on a command
;; binds RFC 4005's own print of the command, which no other document's
;; print shares (docs/constraints.md, Precedence). What a NAS or server
;; decides, an earlier message and the RADIUS side of a translation agent
;; are not in the message, so a rule resting on them is `text-only`.


;; The CER the sentence names too is RFC 6733's command, which this file
;; does not print.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aar-auth-application-id-nasreq
; AVP: Auth-Application-Id
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 1.3
"Diameter applications conforming to this specification MUST advertise support by including the value of one (1) in the Auth-Application-Id of Capabilities-Exchange-Request (CER), AA-Request (AAR), and AA-Answer (AAA) messages."
    range 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aaa-auth-application-id-nasreq
; AVP: Auth-Application-Id
; Command: AA-Answer
; Section: 1.3
"Diameter applications conforming to this specification MUST advertise support by including the value of one (1) in the Auth-Application-Id of Capabilities-Exchange-Request (CER), AA-Request (AAR), and AA-Answer (AAA) messages."
    range 1


;; The State AVPs of the AA-Answer before, an earlier message.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aar-state-from-the-aaa
; AVP: State
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 3.1
"A subsequent AAR message SHOULD be sent, with the User-Password AVP that includes the user's response to the prompt, and MUST include any State AVPs that were present in the AAA message."
    text-only


;; At least one of the two; the Acct-Application-Id the sentence after it
;; has the Vendor-Specific-Application-Id "must" hold, in lower case, is no
;; requirement.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: acr-acct-application-id-or-vendor-specific
; AVP: Acct-Application-Id
; Command: Accounting-Request
; Section: 3.9
"Either of Acct-Application-Id or Vendor-Specific-Application-Id AVPs MUST be present."
    present-if not Vendor-Specific-Application-Id


;; "as it was in the request": which of the two, the request's choice, is
;; not read, the answer's own presence alone.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aca-acct-application-id-or-vendor-specific
; AVP: Acct-Application-Id
; Command: Accounting-Answer
; Section: 3.10
"Either Acct-Application-Id or Vendor-Specific-Application-Id AVPs MUST be present, as it was in the request."
    present-if not Vendor-Specific-Application-Id


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: originating-line-info-octets
; AVP: Originating-Line-Info
; Section: 4.8
"The Value field contains two octets (00 - 99)."
    length 2 octets


;; The AVP carries the clear text: the encryption is the transport's, IPsec
;; or TLS, as the clause says before.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: user-password-length
; AVP: User-Password
; Section: 5.1
"The clear-text password (prior to encryption) MUST NOT be longer than 128 bytes in length."
    length *..128 octets


;; The AA-Request is the one command of the document printing CHAP-Auth.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aar-chap-auth-with-challenge
; AVP: CHAP-Auth
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 5.4
"If the CHAP-Auth AVP is found in a message, the CHAP-Challenge AVP MUST be present as well."
    requires CHAP-Challenge


;; CHAP with MD5 (5), the one value the clause defines.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: chap-auth-md5-response
; AVP: CHAP-Response
; Within: CHAP-Auth
; Section: 5.5
"This algorithm requires that the CHAP-Response AVP MUST be present in the CHAP-Auth AVP."
    present-if CHAP-Algorithm = "CHAP with MD5"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: chap-ident-octet
; AVP: CHAP-Ident
; Section: 5.6
"The CHAP-Ident AVP (AVP Code 404) is of type OctetString and contains the 1 octet CHAP Identifier used in the computation of the CHAP response [PPPCHAP]."
    length 1 octets


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: chap-response-octets
; AVP: CHAP-Response
; Section: 5.7
"The CHAP-Response AVP (AVP Code 405) is of type OctetString and contains the 16 octet authentication data provided by the user in response to the CHAP challenge [PPPCHAP]."
    length 16 octets


;; The AA-Request is the one command of the document printing the three;
;; the clause's "is only present when the Framed-Protocol AVP ... is set to
;; ARAP" has no MUST, and is not read.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aar-arap-password-without-other-passwords
; AVP: ARAP-Password
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 5.9
"This AVP MUST NOT be present if either the User-Password or the CHAP-Auth AVP is present."
    excludes User-Password or CHAP-Auth


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: arap-challenge-response-octets
; AVP: ARAP-Challenge-Response
; Section: 5.10
"This AVP contains an 8 octet response to the dial-in client's challenge."
    length 8 octets


;; The QoSFilterRule's text, which no codec reads.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: qos-filter-rule-format
; AVP: QoS-Filter-Rule
; Section: 6.9
"QoSFilterRule filters MUST follow the following format:"
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: framed-mtu-range
; AVP: Framed-MTU
; Section: 6.10.3
"The MTU value MUST be in the range from 64 to 65535."
    range 64..65535


;; An IPv4 address, four octets, as RADIUS's attribute carries it.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: framed-ip-address-octets
; AVP: Framed-IP-Address
; Section: 6.11.1
"The Framed-IP-Address AVP (AVP Code 8) [RADIUS] is of type OctetString and contains an IPv4 address of the type specified in the attribute value to be configured for the user."
    length 4 octets


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: framed-ip-netmask-octets
; AVP: Framed-IP-Netmask
; Section: 6.11.2
"The Framed-IP-Netmask AVP (AVP Code 9) is of type OctetString and contains the four octets of the IPv4 netmask to be configured for the user when the user is a router to a network."
    length 4 octets


;; The request's OctetString's value, which no condition reads.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aaa-framed-ip-netmask-after-all-ones
; AVP: Framed-IP-Netmask
; Command: AA-Answer
; Section: 6.11.2
"This AVP MUST be present in a response if the request included this AVP with a value of 0xFFFFFFFF."
    text-only


;; A route's text, which no codec reads.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: framed-route-text
; AVP: Framed-Route
; Section: 6.11.3
"The string MUST contain a destination prefix in dotted quad form optionally followed by a slash and a decimal length specifier stating how many high-order bits of the prefix should be used."
    text-only


;; As Framed-Route's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: framed-ipv6-route-text
; AVP: Framed-IPv6-Route
; Section: 6.11.7
"The string MUST contain an IPv6 address prefix followed by a slash and a decimal length specifier stating how many high order bits of the prefix should be used."
    text-only


;; The values the clause defines. Its "MUST only be present in an
;; authorization response" is table 10.1's AA-Request "0", read there, and
;; the Accounting-Request's body prints the AVP (docs/constraints.md).
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: framed-appletalk-link-range
; AVP: Framed-AppleTalk-Link
; Section: 6.13.1
"Despite the size of the field, values range from 0 to 65,535."
    range 0..65535


;; As Framed-AppleTalk-Link's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: framed-appletalk-network-range
; AVP: Framed-AppleTalk-Network
; Section: 6.13.2
"Despite the size of the field, values range from 0 to 65,535."
    range 0..65535


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: login-tcp-port-range
; AVP: Login-TCP-Port
; Section: 6.16.1
"The value MUST NOT be greater than 65,535."
    range 0..65535


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aaa-login-lat-service-for-lat
; AVP: Login-LAT-Service
; Command: AA-Answer
; Section: 6.17.1
"This AVP MUST only be present in the response if the Login-Service AVP states that LAT is desired."
    requires Login-Service = LAT


;; The clause's Login-Service-Type is section 6.15.3's Login-Service.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aaa-login-lat-node-for-lat
; AVP: Login-LAT-Node
; Command: AA-Answer
; Section: 6.17.2
"This AVP MUST only be present in a response if the Login-Service-Type AVP is set to LAT."
    requires Login-Service = LAT


;; As section 6.17.2's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aaa-login-lat-group-for-lat
; AVP: Login-LAT-Group
; Command: AA-Answer
; Section: 6.17.3
"This AVP MUST only be present in a response if the Login-Service-Type AVP is set to LAT."
    requires Login-Service = LAT


;; As section 6.17.2's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aaa-login-lat-port-for-lat
; AVP: Login-LAT-Port
; Command: AA-Answer
; Section: 6.17.4
"This AVP MUST only be present in a response if the Login-Service-Type AVP is set to LAT."
    requires Login-Service = LAT


;; Whether a name other than the default is desired is the server's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: tunnel-client-auth-id-other-than-default
; AVP: Tunnel-Client-Auth-Id
; Within: Tunneling
; Section: 7.10
"This AVP MUST be present in the authorization response if an authentication name other than the default is desired."
    text-only


;; As section 7.10's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: tunnel-server-auth-id-other-than-default
; AVP: Tunnel-Server-Auth-Id
; Within: Tunneling
; Section: 7.11
"This AVP MUST be present in the authorization response if an authentication name other than the default is desired."
    text-only


;; The State an earlier answer carried.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aar-state-returned-unmodified
; AVP: State
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 9.3.4
"If so, the NAS MUST return it unmodified in the subsequent AA-Request command."
"If the NAS performs the Termination-Action by sending a new AA-Request command upon termination of the current service, it MUST return the State AVP unmodified in the new request command."
    text-only


;; Table 10.1's AAR column: what its "0" says the AA-Request never
;; carries, an AVP its body admits only through * [ AVP ]. The table spells
;; Framed-AppleTalk-Link, -Network and -Zone Framed-Appletalk-.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aar-acct-interim-interval-table-absent
; AVP: Acct-Interim-Interval
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 10.1
"0 The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message."
"Acct-Interim-Interval | 0 | 0-1 |"
    absent


